            <ArticleTitle>Gold(i)-catalyzed addition of carboxylic acids to internal alkynes in aqueous medium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1670-1679</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6ob02800d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report herein the efficient hydro-oxycarbonylation of symmetrical and unsymmetrical internal alkynes with carboxylic acids in water at 60 °C, employing the catalytic system [AuCl(PPh3)]/AgOAc (5 mol%). This simple and eco-friendly protocol allows for the synthesis of a wide variety of trisubstituted enol esters (37 examples) in high yields and with complete Z-stereoselectivity. The use of microwave irradiation as an alternative energy source has also been evaluated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
